{
  "schema_version": "prompt-runtime.program-scenario.v1",
  "story_path": "user_stories/prompt-approve-ports.md",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "`approvePromptText` sets the top-level `\"status\"` to `\"approved\"` and `\"prose_sha256\"` to the `compute.hash_utf8` digest of the trimmed prose while leaving nested `\"status\"` fields untouched, and raises `missing-prose-sha256` when `\"prose_sha256\"` is absent."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "`runApprove` in easy mode with valid `said` words verifies that the target is a Git-visible `*.prompt.md` file, writes the approved prompt text, records durable approval evidence via `policy.appendApproval`, prints `Approved prompts/cli/sample.prompt.md.`, and returns `{exitCode: 0}`."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "`runApprove` in strict mode (`strictApprovals: true`) refuses `--said` with `{exitCode: 2}` and `pdd approve is for a person at a terminal.` on `output.stderr` without writing the prompt or recording an approval."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "`runApprove` raises `invalid-approve-cwd` before invoking Git when `cwd` is blank."
    }
  ],
